 =-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/99e3776bfa4048703042970a2479a86c749e3e2a547dce966fceb23b671d66f2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106890/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49c501da-161c-53be-8349-571cc6a07975"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106890"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9df924aa-9f87-522a-9655-5f3f3e055ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "87cf909f-12d3-5fc0-b634-fafe0460db32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "4a1cf072-f5b2-5678-9872-81e48397fd3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4181df71-f3a3-5c22-b1a3-914f4af3f8bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0e8ff9be-1c48-5726-aaaa-4af5ed8d9270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb60fbee-6593-5091-928c-930fcf23a5f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106902/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-106902/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-106902/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-106902/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-106902/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-106902/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106902" :question/id #uuid "4a90b8ce-e812-571d-b6d3-16961f18158d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106902" :question/problem "The eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2k\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =k+2$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ k-1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2k\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ k-1\\end{aligned}] & =(k+2)[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ k-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k+1 \\\\ -2+2{k}^{2}-2k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-k-2 \\\\ {k}^{2}+k-2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2k+1=-k-2, \\\\ -2+2{k}^{2}-2k={k}^{2}+k-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-k=-3\\,⟹\\,k=3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=3$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+2{k}^{2}-2k & ={k}^{2}+k-2 \\\\ -2+2\\cdot (3)^{2}-2\\cdot 3 & =(3)^{2}+3-2 \\\\ 10 & =10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "9032fa7a-07e5-5773-8f28-b6e3b6a3c228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0fbb919a-74de-5e76-a351-93a9af2a2c75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "664946aa-cb50-5385-b252-05759f631373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3821c5d3-7e4f-5757-9b80-a411995b54ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "24f55770-03f9-5dcf-aefd-1ce53ffa437d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18b3c739-5ae2-5776-9cf2-6747ea639499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107842/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-107842/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-107842/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-107842/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-107842/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-107842/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107842" :question/id #uuid "6c8c1613-f0c1-51af-80b3-8266221c5212" :question/math-academy-id "q-107842" :question/problem "The eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8+k \\\\ 3 & 5k\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2k$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -8+k \\\\ 3 & 5k\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =2k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}k-10 \\\\ -6+5k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4k \\\\ 2k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k-10=-4k, \\\\ -6+5k=2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nk-10=-4k\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=2$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6+5k & =2k \\\\ -6+5(2) & =2(2) \\\\ 4 & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "985df5db-1f11-56a4-a917-a84b1394da5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8149b2d9-d323-521f-903c-42b115ae4c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "5097ad64-b06c-5d1f-9671-c6a62c58096b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ee9401c3-c4c7-5492-a6c0-3ec82367ba91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "684e2788-0f2c-572b-8fd5-0410e5364d04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31c46150-14a8-5d7e-81f8-99a46e83ab9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75611/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-75611/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-75611/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-75611/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-75611/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-75611/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75611" :question/id #uuid "1c4e0639-18e2-5768-9e5f-81dd26992565" :question/math-academy-id "q-75611" :question/problem "The eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 20-4k & 3\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2k+1$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 20-4k & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =(2k+1)[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 26-4k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2k+1 \\\\ 4k+2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7=2k+1, \\\\ 26-4k=4k+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n7=2k+1\\,⟹\\,k=3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=3$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}26-4k & =4k+2 \\\\ 26-4\\cdot 3 & =4\\cdot 3+2 \\\\ 14 & =14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75611/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75611"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "9b1ced1c-2e75-52c2-919e-c17afd3a8559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "4b73500b-bfeb-5121-83dc-2bacc3649339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "b87db648-1d01-51d2-adb6-b325ed28cbb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "ebea0d86-1323-5fe5-8869-3a11a6d61a40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "a061c4ae-2b3b-5920-a222-a2cedffb9155" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106945/selec